# A cache filled where it is missing and then read only to check it is not empty: the read decides a choice and goes no
# further, so the route does not use what is there, and the cache stays where the route leaves it.

route fillcheck.run
line entry > run call
line run > File(cache/data.txt) own
line File(cache/data.txt) > run own

# An error is a value (#138): `raise RuntimeError(..)` builds it in the arm that raises it, the error the arm hands on is
# one value at the choice's moment, and the route's border hands it on.
choice run/?1                                                        # if CACHE.read_text() == ""
step run/?1/RuntimeError()
line run/?1/RuntimeError() > RuntimeError@run/?1 value
line RuntimeError@run/?1 > run value
line run > RuntimeError@run value
home RuntimeError@run/?1 run
home RuntimeError@run run

side entry left
side File(cache/data.txt) right
